[25.140466, "o", "R1_ARM=PC R1_ENTRY=coordinator R1_ROUTES=coordinator=cloud,implementor=local,verifier=local,plan=cloud,implement=local,critique=local,smol=local M2_LOCAL_REPLAY=false\r\n"]
[95.498534, "o", "  │ All entries present. Now the inheritance proof with real users.\r\n[approval] bash: runuser -u alice -- sh -c 'umask 002; echo hi > /srv/shared/alice-test.txt; mkdir /srv/shared/alice-dir'; echo \"alice-exit=$?\"\r\nrunuser -u bob -- sh -c 'cat /srv/shared/alice-test.txt; echo more >> /srv/shared/alice-test.txt; echo ok > /srv/shared/alice-dir/bob-test.txt'; echo \"bob-exit=$?\"\r\ngetfacl -p /srv/shared/alice-test.txt\r\ngetfacl -p /srv/shared/alice-dir\r\nstat -c '%A %a %U %G' /srv/shared/alice-test.txt /srv/shared/alice-dir — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash runuser -u alice -- sh -c 'umask 002; echo hi > /srv/shared/alice-test…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 5 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Inheritance works: bob read `hi` and appended, wrote into alice's dir. No…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /srv/shared/alice-test.txt /srv/shared/alice-dir\r\necho \"ls-A-output-start\"; ls -A /srv/shared; echo \"ls-A-output-end\"\r\nid nobody >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"nobody exists\" || echo \"nobody missing\"\r\nrunuser -u nobody -- ls /srv/shared; echo \"exit=$?\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /srv/shared/alice-test.txt /srv/shared/alice-dir echo \"ls-A-out…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 6 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ glob \r\n    ✓ glob scripts/* — 1 file(s)\r\n  ⚙ read scripts/setup-shared-acl.sh\r\n    ✓ read scripts/setup-shared-acl.sh — 33 lines\r\nDone.\r\n\r\n**Changed:** added `scripts/setup-shared-acl.sh` — an idempotent, root-run script that creates group `research` and users `alice`/`bob` (adding both to the group), creates `/srv/shared`, sets group `research` + `chmod 2770`, then applies the access ACL (`u::rwx,g::rwx,g:research:rwx,u:alice:rwx,u:bob:rwx,m::rwx,o::---`) and the identical default ACL for inheritance. I then ran it against the host.\r\n\r\n**Live state (from the run):**\r\n- `stat /srv/shared` → `drwxrws--- 2770 root research` — setgid bit and mode present.\r\n- `getfacl /srv/shared` shows exactly the required seven access entries plus the seven matching `default:` entries, mask `rwx`, `other::---`.\r\n- Inheritance proven with the real users, then removed: alice created a file and a subdir; bob read *and* appended to alice's file and wrote into alice's subdir; the subdir came out `drwxrws--- 2770 alice research` carrying the full default ACL; alice's file inherited `user:bob:rwx` (effective `rw-` because a plain new file has no execute bit — that is file-creation semantics, not a mask clamp).\r\n- `nobody` (not in `research`): `ls: cannot open directory '/srv/shared': Permission denied`, exit 2.\r\n- Cleanup verified: `ls -A /srv/shared` prints nothing, so the directory is empty for the tests.\r\n\r\n**Not done:** nothing committed (no repo history involved); `/srv/shared` lives on the host, the script is the reproducible record of it.\r\n\r\n[result] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=9 surface=adbe4e271f4b\r\n"]
